{
  "requirement": "Repository validation MUST continue after a failed check and report every failed\ncheck it finds in one run, each as a {term}`requirements.ci.validation_error`.\nThis is a convention for every validation error; the requirement for each check\nstates which conditions that check reports. A file that cannot be parsed, such as\na malformed `habeas.toml`, `book.toml`, or evidence file, is one failed check:\nits error MAY report only the first parse or decoding problem in that file, and\nchecks that do not depend on its contents MUST still run.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Judgment: the requirement is satisfied.** The implementation does what it states, the {impl} marking is adequate, and the tests cover the main cases.\n\n**Implementation**\n- **Collecting errors.** `inspect_repository_with_progress` (src/evidence.rs 172–301) keeps one `errors` vector and runs every stage in turn. The stages are workspace config, book source, definitions, evidence files, missing-evidence coverage, reference collection and validation, and Rust item coverage. A failure in one stage is pushed to the vector and never stops the next. The `io::Result` return is only for failing to canonicalize the root, which is not a check.\n- **Malformed `habeas.toml`.** It is recorded as a single error (`load_workspace_evidence` error pushed at ~line 181), and the later checks still run. `main` (src/main.rs 113–127) deliberately skips the early workspace-config bail-out for `status` and `info`, so those commands print the report instead of aborting.\n- **Malformed `book.toml`.** `book_source_dir` (303–357) pushes one error for an unreadable file, invalid TOML, or a bad `book.src`. It then falls back to `md`, so definition collection and the later checks still run.\n- **Malformed evidence file.** `validate_evidence_file` (587–723) returns after the first read, JSON-parse or not-an-object problem, which the requirement allows (\"MAY report only the first parse or decoding problem\"). For a well-formed record it reports every failed field check, every dependency problem and every bad input.\n- **Other stages.** These also continue past failures:\n  - `collect_definitions` (359–506) handles invalid names, missing fences, duplicates, empty text and bad options by pushing an error and moving on.\n  - `files_with_extension` (526–585) pushes an error and continues past unreadable directories or entries.\n  - `close_dependencies` and `validate_dependencies` (src/terms.rs) report one problem per unresolvable term.\n  - `validate_references`, `collect_references_with_progress` and `rust_coverage::validate_rust_functions` also continue after each error.\n- **{impl} marking.** The functions that enforce or exercise continuation carry `{impl}` for `requirements.ci.errors`. `validate_references`, `collect_references_with_progress` and `rust_coverage::validate_rust_functions` also continue after errors but are not marked for this requirement. Because it is a cross-cutting convention and the marked functions carry the central behaviour, I do not count that as a gap. `DefinitionKind::noun` is also marked; it only supplies the wording used in the messages, so that mark is marginal.\n\n**Tests**\n- `collects_missing_orphan_format_false_and_changed_line_errors` (src/evidence.rs 1782) creates many simultaneous failures and asserts that all of them are reported in one run. They include a malformed evidence file, an orphan, missing evidence, changed text, a false determination, many bad input forms, a duplicate definition and an empty definition.\n- `configuration_and_dependency_failures_do_not_stop_later_checks` (2073) covers these cases:\n  - several unresolvable terms are all reported;\n  - other records are still checked;\n  - an invalid `habeas.toml` and a malformed `book.toml` are each reported;\n  - a malformed evidence file and an unknown source reference are still reported.\n- `inspection_progress_preserves_validation_and_finishes_each_phase` (1578) mixes a broken evidence file with an unparsable Rust source and checks that the other findings are still reported.\n- `status_loads_nearest_workspace_file_without_validating_authoring` (tests/commands.rs 199) checks that `status` and `info` report an invalid `habeas.toml` and also report an unrelated malformed evidence file.\n- `book_source_defaults_only_when_absent_and_reports_invalid_configuration` is marked for `ci.book_source`, not this requirement. It does check the individual `book.toml` error variants, including `book.src` set to `''`, an absolute path and `../outside`.\n\nNo FIXME or acknowledged gaps were found.",
  "references": "73d3cce44ea4f31abae83f98f96c05ebc5a843fdf5b71f871ecf557755cae031",
